\title{\textbf{Candidate Transcriptional Metabolic States in Meningioma scRNA-seq Data}}
\author{QA_R9 Research Analysis}
\date{\today}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\section{Data and Methods}

This analysis uses single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (3CA:20773) \url{https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8}, comprising 58,843 cells and 33,538 genes from 10 meningioma samples. User-supplied metabolic genes (1,988 symbols in \texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv}) were matched to the expression matrix via exact-symbol aggregation, yielding 1,646 genes after prevalence filtering.
